cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ile-predict: A structure-based prediction system for intravenous lipid emulsion amenability in acute poisoning"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the ADMET-AI paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tatlı"
    given-names: "Mehmet"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5907-9161"
    affiliation: "Department of Emergency Medicine, University of Health Sciences, Van Training and Research Hospital, Van, Türkiye; Department of Neuroscience (PhD Programme), Van Yüzüncü Yıl University, Van, Türkiye"
abstract: >-
  ile-predict estimates how amenable a toxic agent is to intravenous lipid
  emulsion (ILE, "lipid rescue") therapy directly from chemical structure.
  Physicochemical descriptors are predicted with ADMET-AI, and a logistic model
  calibrated against a 76-drug literature-consensus responder / non-responder
  reference set converts effective lipophilicity (logD7.4) into a probability of
  ILE responsiveness. Research and education prototype; not a clinical decision
  tool.
